# What never enters the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile only ever COPYs from the context, so a file excluded here
# cannot end up in a layer — not by a careless `COPY . .`, not by a future
# edit to the Dockerfile, not by anyone. That is the whole reason .env is
# listed: a secret that cannot enter the build context cannot end up in an
# image. Anything the server needs at run time arrives through `docker run -e`
# or a mounted file, never through the context.

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*

# Dependencies — the image installs its own from the lockfile, so a host
# node_modules (wrong platform, wrong node, possibly stale) must not leak in.
node_modules

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Build output and test residue — the image builds its own dist/ from source.
dist
coverage
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Docker's own files
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
